# {{ name }}

A dependency-free web starter for {{ display_name }}, generated by toolkit_engine {{ foundation_version }}.
It is a branded app shell (header band, a sample card with buttons, chips and status badges, footer
with the support link) served by a small TypeScript static server. These files are managed: regenerate
the workspace instead of editing them. Put your own screens in new files beside them.

## Requirements

Node.js 22.18 or newer (including 24). Node runs the `.ts` files directly by stripping types, so there is
**no install step**: no `npm install`, no build, no packages. Node 22.6 to 22.17 can also run them with
`--experimental-strip-types`; older versions cannot.

## Run

From this folder (`apps/{{ name }}`):

```powershell
npm start
```

or `node server.ts`, then open <http://127.0.0.1:5173/>. Set `PORT` to use another port
(`$env:PORT = "8080"` in PowerShell).

The server binds to 127.0.0.1 only, so it is not reachable from other machines. It serves the `public`
folder, answers only `GET`, returns 404 for anything outside `public` (including `..` and `%2e%2e`
paths, dot-files and symbolic links that lead out), and sends `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'`
and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`. The page therefore has no inline script or style.

## Test

```powershell
npm test
```

runs `node --test` against `test/server.test.ts`: an ephemeral-port server, the security headers, traversal
and method checks, and a check that the shell has no inline script or style.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `server.ts` | The static server (erasable TypeScript: no enums, namespaces, parameter properties or decorators) |
| `test/server.test.ts` | `node:test` and `node:assert` tests |
| `public/index.html` | The app shell |
| `public/theme.css` | Generated from the firm's design tokens and component choices, the same source as the workspace HTML guide |
| `public/app.js` | A small plain ES module. Browsers cannot run TypeScript, so client code is JavaScript and the server and tests are TypeScript |
| `public/assets/` | The firm's brand SVGs |
| `public/fonts/` | Packaged brand fonts with their licenses, when the firm has any |
| `tsconfig.json` | For editors only. Node never reads it |

## Optional: type-check

Node strips types without checking them. To check them, install TypeScript yourself:

```powershell
npm install -D typescript @types/node
npx tsc
```

Nothing in `npm start` or `npm test` needs it, and this starter does not install it for you.

## Identity

The package name (`{{ name }}`) comes from `technical.namespace` and never changes when the firm is
rebranded. The display name, logo text and support link follow `identity` in the firm configuration.
